window.docContents[69].resolve({"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.LibsignalCli.Kyber1024Delta/#file-Computational___Specifications___LibsignalCli___Kyber1024Delta":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/LibsignalCli › Kyber1024Delta.leanTier 1 · statement file\n\nTier 1 · statement file used by the computational proof 1 headline theorem depend on it 59 lines trust banner B1, trusted: the statement source ↗Read in full. A statement file: its definitions say what the headline theorems claim (games, adversaries, bounds). Proofs are cut after := and shown as ⋯; Lean checks them.\n\n\n\nConcrete Round-3 CRYSTALS-Kyber-1024 δ_kem Correctness Statement (Kyber1024Delta)Trusted: the statement. States Kyber1024KemDeltaCorrect: at realPEParams (W.Q.encaps = kyber1024EncapsVec, W.Q.decaps = kyber1024DecapsVec) and kemKeyGen = kyber1024KemKeyGen, the PQXDH model primitives modelPrims (realUnreachedPrims kyber1024KemKeyGen) realPEParams satisfy both the wire-length validity premise _hKemValid (1568-byte public keys, 3168-byte secret keys) and, for any ε with KyberNoiseGap ε, the δ_kem-correctness premise KemDeltaCorrect P (ε + 1 / 2 ^ 112) of CliPqxdhSecurityForAnyKem (StatementPqElfAnyKem.lean), instantiating δ_kem = ε + 1 / 2 ^ 112 in the Main Theorem CliPqxdhSecurityFor (StatementPqElf.lean, DEV-PQ21).Unlike the heuristic 2^-174 figure in the Kyber v3.02 specification (which treats compression rounding errors as uniform and independent), 1 / 2 ^ 112 holds rigorously over every SampleNTT (SHAKE-128) matrix Â (with no uniformity assumption on SHAKE-128), concrete SHA3-256 message hash, exact Compress_{11,5,1} / Decompress_{11,5,1} rounding, and Fujisaki–Okamoto re-encryption, assuming only KyberNoiseGap ε (proved by kyber1024_kem_delta_correct in Computational/Theorems/Lemmas.lean).\n\n\n\ndef Kyber1024KemDeltaCorrectL45–57 ↗#Concrete Round-3 CRYSTALS-Kyber-1024 key-generation length validity ((1568B, 3168B)) and δ_kem = ε + 1 / 2 ^ 112 decapsulation-failure bound for modelPrims (realUnreachedPrims kyber1024KemKeyGen) realPEParams under KyberNoiseGap ε, discharging _hKemValid and _hKemBin of CliPqxdhSecurityForAnyKem (StatementPqElfAnyKem.lean) to establish CliPqxdhSecurityFor (StatementPqElf.lean).\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/LibsignalCli/Kyber1024Delta.lean","id":"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.LibsignalCli.Kyber1024Delta/#file-Computational___Specifications___LibsignalCli___Kyber1024Delta"}});